# Claude Code path-scoped rule files: keep their YAML front matter LF on every checkout.
# If Claude Code failed to parse a CRLF front matter it would load the file in EVERY session,
# which is exactly what these files exist to avoid (docs/design/2026-09-30-lean-claude-md-design.md).
# '**/' also matches no folder, so this covers .claude/rules/*.md and any subfolder Claude Code discovers.
# ClaudeContextBudgetTests checks the bytes too (no CRLF, no byte-order mark).
.claude/rules/**/*.md text eol=lf
